ms deserve the same per-function production\ncards: pronoun choice (tag production-which-pronoun), Perfekt vs Präteritum,\nwissen vs kennen, wenn/wann/als/ob, and similar.\n\nWORKED EXAMPLES\n(Preposition cards shown; other cards like verbs/nouns also apply.)\n\nInput: "Am Wochenende fahren wir in die Berge."\nPrepositions present: an (am), in.\n  - vocabulary: "an"   tags: ["preposition"]\n  - vocabulary: "in"   tags: ["preposition"]\n  - grammar (production-which-preposition):\n      "Choosing 'when': an (days/parts of week) / in (months, seasons, periods)\n       / um (clock times)"\n       → am Wochenende uses an because it's a part of the week\n  - grammar (production-which-preposition):\n      "Choosing 'to a place': nach/zu/in/auf/an"\n       → in die Berge uses in: an area you move into, takes an article\n\nInput: "Im Sommer fliege ich zu meiner Schwester."\nPrepositions present: in (im), zu.\n  - vocabulary: "in"   tags: ["preposition"]\n  - vocabulary: "zu"   tags: ["preposition"]\n  - grammar (production-which-preposition):\n      "Choosing 'when': an (days/parts of week) / in (months, seasons, periods)\n       / um (clock times)"\n       → im Sommer uses in: a season   [reuse/link the card from above]\n  - grammar (production-which-preposition):\n      "Choosing 'to a place': nach/zu/in/auf/an"\n       → zu meiner Schwester uses zu: destination is a person\n       [reuse/link the same destination card]\n\nUSER CONTEXT\nNative language: English. German level: roughly A2.	2026-06-17 20:26:38.895586+00
